        <section>
            <h2>Conclusion</h2>
            <p>The internet connects devices and people through a system of networks, servers, routers and communication protocols. DNS helps browsers locate websites, while packets carry information between devices. These processes happen in seconds, making online communication feel simple. Learning how the internet works also encourages us to think about privacy, security and responsible use. As technology continues to develop, understanding these fundamentals will remain useful for students and anyone who uses digital services.</p>
